\details{
\strong{Input.} One row per gene, as written by limma (\code{topTable()}), DESeq2 (\code{results()}) or edgeR
(\code{topTags()}). The gene column is found by its name (\code{gene}, \code{symbol}, \code{SYMBOL}, \code{gene_name},
\code{ID}, \code{ensembl_gene_id}, \code{entrez}, ...) or taken from the row names, and may hold gene symbols,
Ensembl gene IDs or Entrez IDs; the last two are mapped to symbols with org.Hs.eg.db. Genes are
ranked by a signed test statistic (\code{t}, \code{stat}, ...); without one, by sign(log fold change) times
-log10(P value) (\code{logFC} or \code{log2FoldChange} with \code{P.Value}, \code{pvalue} or \code{PValue}). When a gene
occurs more than once, the row with the largest absolute statistic is kept. Give the full table of
tested genes, not only the significant ones.

\strong{Scoring.} Both libraries are scored with \code{\link[=run_l1000_pai]{run_l1000_pai()}} in paired mode (fgsea, gene sets of
10-500 genes, eps 1e-10, observed-tail P values, Benjamini-Hochberg adjustment over pairs; a call
needs |activity score| >= 1, a coherent adjusted P value < 0.05 and both arms aligned).
Pathways come from \code{\link[=pai_enrich]{pai_enrich()}} (over-representation among the Activated and the Inhibited
targets) or, when no term is significant, from \code{\link[=pai_gsea_pathways]{pai_gsea_pathways()}}. Compound mechanisms come
from the Chem taxonomy 3.0.1 (\code{\link[=get_l1000_annotation_catalog]{get_l1000_annotation_catalog()}}) and drug families from
\code{\link[=pai_familyplot]{pai_familyplot()}}.

\strong{Pages.} Overview, key findings, quality checks and how to read the calls; input check and
proliferation signal; gene knockouts; evidence of the top gene calls (\code{\link[=pai_evidence_card]{pai_evidence_card()}} and the
leading-edge network \code{\link[=pai_cnetplot]{pai_cnetplot()}}); pathways; pathway enrichment in depth; compounds; evidence
of the top compound calls (the same two displays); drug families and mechanism classes; flags and
notes; methods, versions and references. The pathway enrichment pages depend on the pathway result: with terms
over-represented among the calls, nine pages: \code{\link[=pai_enrichplot]{pai_enrichplot()}}; \code{\link[=pai_gobubble]{pai_gobubble()}} with
\code{\link[=pai_term_cnetplot]{pai_term_cnetplot()}}; \code{\link[=pai_gocircle]{pai_gocircle()}} (top 10, all members, labelled); \code{\link[=pai_gochord]{pai_gochord()}} with
\code{\link[=pai_govenn]{pai_govenn()}}; \code{\link[=pai_gobar]{pai_gobar()}} with \code{\link[=pai_gocluster]{pai_gocluster()}}; \code{\link[=pai_goheat]{pai_goheat()}}; \code{\link[=pai_armmap]{pai_armmap()}}; and, for each
direction, \code{\link[=pai_hubplot]{pai_hubplot()}} with \code{\link[=pai_emapplot]{pai_emapplot()}}, then \code{\link[=pai_chordplot]{pai_chordplot()}} with \code{\link[=pai_enrich_cnetplot]{pai_enrich_cnetplot()}}. With only the ranked test,
the two hub pages from \code{\link[=pai_gsea_pathways]{pai_gsea_pathways()}}; without pathways, none. \code{enrichment = "core"} keeps
the first two and the hub genes.

\strong{Checks.} Each check is OK, Check or Caution: gene coverage of the signature genes (>= 90\%,= 70\%, lower); number of CRISPR calls (>= 10, 1-9, 0); share of Discordant pairs in eitherlibrary (<= 10\%, <= 30\%, higher); a proliferation signal in the input (Hallmark E2F targets orG2M checkpoint with adjusted P < 0.05 and |NES| >= 2 gives Check); common hits among the 20strongest compound calls (<= 3, 4-6, more); called genes absent from the input among the 20strongest gene calls (<= 2, 3-5, more); and whether pathways are over-represented among the calls(OK) or only the ranked test is available (Check).

\strong{Common hits.} A compound is a common hit when it is called at the end where it usually sits
in unrelated experiments: its median percentile over 12 public GEO perturbation contrasts (9 groups;
listed in \code{system.file("extdata", "report", "README.md", package = "L1000PAI")}) is >= 0.80 and it
is Concordant here, or <= 0.20 and it is Opposing.

\strong{First run.} The L1000 libraries are downloaded and verified through L1000PAIdata (about 32 MB)
and the KEGG and Reactome gene-set libraries are downloaded from Enrichr into the cache; GO gene
sets are built from org.Hs.eg.db. Later runs work offline from the caches. A run takes 4-5
minutes, most of it scoring, and needs about 6 GB of free memory.

The Hallmark E2F targets and G2M checkpoint gene sets shipped with the package are from MSigDB
(CC BY 4.0; Liberzon et al., Cell Systems 2015).
